WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.060
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:03.330 --> 00:05.950
Private Kim Hyeon Uk. Left-high shot, all clear.

3
00:05.950 --> 00:09.310
- Cycle the bolt two or three times. - Cycling the bolt two or three times.

4
00:09.310 --> 00:11.870
- Check the chamber. - Checking chamber. Chamber is clear.

5
00:11.870 --> 00:14.210
- Shoulder arms. - Shoulder arms.

6
00:14.210 --> 00:16.270
- Selector to semi. - Selector to semi.

7
00:16.270 --> 00:17.670
- Fire. - Fire.

8
00:17.670 --> 00:19.290
Trigger pull, all clear.

9
00:19.290 --> 00:20.727
Fire!

10
00:25.400 --> 00:27.483
- What was that? - What?

11
00:28.153 --> 00:30.030
Was that a gunshot?

12
00:30.030 --> 00:33.450
- Hey! Stay still. Let go. Sit down. - Yes, sir.

13
00:33.450 --> 00:34.930
Hey, what are you doing!

14
00:34.930 --> 00:37.371
Hey! Park Min Seok, go and get the assistant platoon leader. Now!

15
00:37.371 --> 00:38.950
- Hurry! - Yes, sir!

16
00:38.950 --> 00:43.220
You, come here. Sit down. Stay still. Got it?

17
00:46.470 --> 00:48.940
- Hey! - P-Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

18
00:58.767 --> 01:00.550
Assistant Platoon Leader! We have a problem!

19
01:00.550 --> 01:01.853
What is it?

20
01:01.853 --> 01:03.814
- Well... outside... - Speak up, you punk. What happened?

21
01:03.814 --> 01:05.800
While... while checking the guns...

22
01:05.800 --> 01:07.390
This little bastard...

23
01:07.390 --> 01:09.370
This is the command center. This is the command center!

24
01:09.370 --> 01:11.870
Gunfire confirmed within the unit! Gunfire confirmed within the unit!

25
01:11.870 --> 01:15.820
Report the current situation immediately! Report the current situation immediately!

26
01:16.590 --> 01:20.375
Yes. Communications are secure. Yes, this is the officer on duty.

27
01:20.375 --> 01:21.811
Yes, I understand.

28
01:28.630 --> 01:30.867
Yes, Company Commander.

29
01:30.867 --> 01:34.459
I've alerted the command center and called the battalion commander.

30
01:34.459 --> 01:37.730
[Incident/Accident Report]

31
01:37.730 --> 01:39.990
Yes. This was the senior on duty, Corporal Park Min Seok.

32
01:39.990 --> 01:44.250
Yes. I will personally conduct the firearm safety inspections from now on.

33
01:44.250 --> 01:46.360
Yes, keep up the good work. Chungseong.

34
01:52.946 --> 01:56.347
I've confirmed everyone who woke up is back in bed.

35
01:56.347 --> 01:58.910
I've briefed the 1st Squad.

36
01:58.910 --> 02:00.829
Good job.

37
02:00.829 --> 02:02.497
- Dong Woo. - Corporal Kim Dong Woo.

38
02:02.497 --> 02:04.410
I'll handle the next shift change myself.

39
02:04.410 --> 02:06.608
Understood. I'm sorry.

40
02:06.608 --> 02:10.450
Oh, Min Seok. What a mess.

41
02:10.450 --> 02:12.675
Corporal Park Min Seok. I'm sorry.

42
02:12.675 --> 02:16.110
Don't be. Just finish up and go to sleep.

43
02:16.110 --> 02:18.077
Yes, sir.

44
02:18.953 --> 02:20.670
What is it?

45
02:20.670 --> 02:23.450
Oh, it's nothing. I'll go back to my post.

46
02:23.450 --> 02:25.190
Right. Good work.

47
02:25.190 --> 02:26.732
Yes, sir. Take care.

48
02:28.148 --> 02:34.112
- What did that punk learn at boot camp? - Who's his senior?

49
02:34.112 --> 02:40.285
- Hey, stop whispering and wait quietly. - Yes, sir!

50
02:40.285 --> 02:44.750
[EP03. Firing Range Rhapsody]

51
02:44.750 --> 02:46.620
Unit, attention!

52
02:46.620 --> 02:48.375
Salute the Company Commander!

53
02:48.375 --> 02:51.167
- Chungseong! Love you! - Chungseong! Love you!

54
02:51.167 --> 02:52.490
Chungseong! Love you!

55
02:52.490 --> 02:54.824
Skip the report. Anyone missing?

56
02:54.824 --> 02:56.550
- No, sir! - No, sir!

57
02:56.550 --> 02:58.218
As you've heard,

58
02:58.218 --> 03:03.410
a blank was fired during a safety inspection at the main entrance.

59
03:03.410 --> 03:07.507
Don't try to find out who did it, and don't harass them for waking you up.

60
03:07.507 --> 03:08.647
Oh, this bastard...

61
03:08.647 --> 03:11.121
- Got it? Choi Byeong Nam. - Huh? Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam!

62
03:11.121 --> 03:12.810
Oh, I wouldn't do that.

63
03:12.810 --> 03:16.406
Right. Make sure no one under Byeong Nam does it either. Got it?

64
03:16.406 --> 03:18.670
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

65
03:18.670 --> 03:20.790
But do you think we'll still have shooting drills in this atmosphere?

66
03:20.790 --> 03:23.730
Yes, we're shooting, Chan Seok. We have to do what we have to do.

67
03:23.730 --> 03:25.130
I'm sorry, sir!

68
03:25.130 --> 03:31.154
Let's consider the dawn incident bad luck and stay alert so it doesn't happen again.

69
03:31.154 --> 03:33.381
- Got it? - Yes, sir!

70
03:33.381 --> 03:37.430
To help us stay alert, shall we go for a run?

71
03:37.430 --> 03:40.804
- Quiet. On Kim Sang Hun! - On Sergeant Kim Sang Hun!

72
03:40.804 --> 03:42.097
Assemble in running formation!

73
03:42.097 --> 03:44.084
- One, two, hey! - One, two, hey!

74
03:45.870 --> 03:49.662
Let's run until we're sweaty and get our heads in the game!

75
03:49.662 --> 03:55.260
Well, running doesn't actually make you alert, so let's skip the run!

76
03:56.820 --> 04:01.890
Instead, let's do the safety inspection exactly ten times by the book before we eat.

77
04:03.170 --> 04:07.610
Guys, no matter how much you slack off, you never slack off on safety.

78
04:07.610 --> 04:09.875
- Got it? - Yes, sir.

79
04:09.875 --> 04:10.987
That's all!

80
04:10.987 --> 04:13.930
Unit, attention! Chungseong! Love you!

81
04:13.930 --> 04:17.220
Chungseong! Love you! Dismissed.

82
04:18.050 --> 04:20.000
Squad leaders, go get the armory keys.

83
04:20.000 --> 04:21.060
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

84
04:21.060 --> 04:24.030
We'll do the safety inspections and get to work.

85
04:24.030 --> 04:25.290
This is annoying. Let's go.

86
04:25.290 --> 04:26.350
Yes, sir.

87
04:26.350 --> 04:27.890
- Ready arms. - Ready arms.

88
04:27.890 --> 04:30.521
- Safety on. - Safety on.

89
04:30.521 --> 04:32.770
- Remove magazine. - Remove magazine.

90
04:32.770 --> 04:34.970
- Lock bolt to the rear. - Lock bolt to the rear.

91
04:34.970 --> 04:37.444
- Check chamber. - Chamber clear.

92
04:37.444 --> 04:40.290
- Cycle bolt two or three times. - Cycle bolt two or three times.

93
04:40.290 --> 04:42.083
- Shoulder arms. - Shoulder arms.

94
04:42.083 --> 04:43.371
- Selector to semi. - Selector to semi.

95
04:43.371 --> 04:45.739
- Fire. - Fire. Trigger function normal.

96
04:45.739 --> 04:48.652
- Again, replace magazine. - Replace magazine.

97
04:48.652 --> 04:50.430
- Ready arms. - Ready arms.

98
04:50.430 --> 04:52.190
- Remove magazine. - Remove magazine.

99
04:52.190 --> 04:53.950
- Lock bolt to the rear. - Lock bolt to the rear.

100
04:53.950 --> 04:56.850
- Check chamber. - Chamber clear.

101
04:56.850 --> 04:59.610
- Cycle bolt two or three times. - Cycle bolt two or three times.

102
04:59.610 --> 05:01.510
- Selector to semi. - Selector to semi.

103
05:01.510 --> 05:02.890
- Shoulder arms. - Shoulder arms.

104
05:02.890 --> 05:05.319
- Fire. - Fire. Trigger function normal.

105
05:05.319 --> 05:07.730
I'm suffering at the end of my service because of that total screw-up.

106
05:07.730 --> 05:09.040
I agree, sir.

107
05:09.040 --> 05:11.630
I thought he was an ace, but he's a total disaster.

108
05:11.630 --> 05:13.710
- Ready arms. - Ready arms.

109
05:13.710 --> 05:15.649
- Remove magazine. - Remove magazine.

110
05:15.649 --> 05:18.443
- Lock bolt to the rear. - Lock bolt to the rear.

111
05:19.834 --> 05:21.630
[Byeon Hyeok Jin]

112
05:30.970 --> 05:33.810
You're giving me quite a rough welcome as soon as I arrive.

113
05:33.810 --> 05:37.773
I'm sorry. I'll retrain them to prevent a recurrence.

114
05:45.220 --> 05:47.264
Right.

115
05:47.264 --> 05:51.765
Well, accidental blank discharges have always been a common issue.

116
05:52.978 --> 05:54.570
But...

117
05:54.570 --> 05:58.510
If the muzzle was directed towards a person, not up,

118
05:58.510 --> 06:00.768
that would've been a big problem, right?

119
06:00.768 --> 06:03.058
Yes, you're right, sir.

120
06:03.058 --> 06:06.558
Big accidents don't happen out of the blue.

121
06:06.558 --> 06:10.788
Small signs are ignored, and then they fester and explode...

122
06:11.458 --> 06:13.078
Platoon leader.

123
06:13.078 --> 06:14.291
Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin!

124
06:14.291 --> 06:18.795
Did you give Private Kim Hyeon Uk safety inspection training yourself?

125
06:18.795 --> 06:19.801
No, sir.

126
06:19.801 --> 06:21.978
Officer of the Day, what about Sergeant First Class Im Seong Min?

127
06:21.978 --> 06:24.831
Sergeant First Class Im Seong Min! I haven't, sir.

128
06:24.831 --> 06:26.658
What about the Company Commander?

129
06:26.658 --> 06:29.728
I'm sorry, sir. I failed to oversee it properly.

130
06:32.978 --> 06:38.700
Who should be the final one to check everything that happens in the unit?

131
06:40.442 --> 06:43.838
The officers. The commanders.

132
06:43.838 --> 06:46.618
If a soldier makes a mistake, that's an accident.

133
06:46.618 --> 06:49.678
But if an officer misses it,

134
06:49.678 --> 06:52.008
that's a matter of responsibility.

135
06:54.618 --> 06:57.278
What do you think we should do, 2nd Company Commander?

136
06:57.278 --> 07:03.181
Yes, we'll strengthen safety inspections and have officers check personally so...

137
07:03.181 --> 07:05.399
That's not what I'm talking about...

138
07:08.387 --> 07:10.378
I'm talking about accountability.

139
07:10.378 --> 07:12.558
Are you just going to let this slide?

140
07:12.558 --> 07:16.019
Disciplining a soldier for this incident seems...

141
07:16.019 --> 07:21.149
Right? If we discipline a soldier for this, our unit is behind the times.

142
07:21.149 --> 07:25.362
Responsibility starts at the top. The commanders should take the blame.

143
07:29.241 --> 07:32.951
Do you understand what I'm saying, 2nd Company Commander?

144
07:33.698 --> 07:35.083
Yes, sir.

145
07:39.751 --> 07:41.215
Good.

146
07:43.297 --> 07:44.985
You may go.

147
07:50.698 --> 07:52.328
Scared you, didn't I?

148
07:53.898 --> 07:58.558
- I'm sorry. - You okay? You and Min Seok are a bad match.

149
07:58.558 --> 08:00.698
So... what's going to happen now?

150
08:00.698 --> 08:04.234
The Company Commander will probably try to let it slide as much as possible.

151
08:04.234 --> 08:06.735
But I don't know about the new battalion commander...

152
08:06.735 --> 08:08.780
Demerit points?

153
08:08.780 --> 08:10.407
Won't it be detention?

154
08:10.407 --> 08:14.229
- Maximum detention? - Oh, stop joking around.

155
08:14.911 --> 08:17.738
Park Min Seok. I heard you're going to detention.

156
08:17.738 --> 08:19.248
Me?

157
08:19.248 --> 08:23.408
- Just kidding. I'm sorry. - That's not funny.

158
08:27.257 --> 08:29.698
- Corporal Park Min Seok. - Yeah?

159
08:29.698 --> 08:32.092
They said you should get ready to go to detention.

160
08:32.092 --> 08:34.013
Really?

161
08:34.013 --> 08:37.111
- Psych! I'm so sorry. - Seriously...

162
08:37.111 --> 08:39.838
Sung Yoon Mo, you bastard! Do you want to die? Are you crazy?

163
08:39.838 --> 08:42.438
Hey, I made him do it. It feels like you're yelling at me, you punk.

164
08:42.438 --> 08:44.548
I'm off.

165
08:44.548 --> 08:46.106
Good work, sir.

166
08:48.528 --> 08:51.592
Nothing bad will happen, right?

167
08:51.592 --> 08:53.078
Don't worry, man.

168
08:53.078 --> 08:54.878
Corporal Park Min Seok.

169
08:54.878 --> 08:56.661
I'm sorry. This is all because of me.

170
08:56.661 --> 09:00.791
No, it's fine. I told you it's okay. Don't worry.

171
09:01.758 --> 09:06.361
Corporal Park Min Seok, Private Kim Hyeon Uk, report to the Company Commander's office.

172
09:08.098 --> 09:10.758
- We'll be back. - Don't worry. Go on.

173
09:10.758 --> 09:13.718
- Yes, sir. - Take care.

174
09:13.718 --> 09:18.038
Don't be discouraged. Good luck, son.

175
09:18.038 --> 09:19.142
Yes, sir!

176
09:19.142 --> 09:21.755
Hey, let's go. Don't be nervous.

177
09:23.883 --> 09:25.188
Hyeon Uk.

178
09:25.188 --> 09:26.718
Private Kim Hyeon Uk.

179
09:26.718 --> 09:32.098
Remember what I said at the bathhouse? We're family, so we stick together.

180
09:32.098 --> 09:34.423
Remember when I said not to try too hard?

181
09:34.423 --> 09:35.858
Yes, sir.

182
09:35.858 --> 09:37.035
Right!

183
09:37.035 --> 09:42.758
Even if you mess up, people will support you, so don't be so intimidated!

184
09:42.758 --> 09:45.176
Yes, sir.

185
09:45.918 --> 09:48.078
- Min Seok. - Corporal Park Min Seok!

186
09:48.078 --> 09:52.018
It's not easy being a senior, is it? Getting called in because of your junior.

187
09:52.018 --> 09:54.158
No, sir. It's fine.

188
09:54.158 --> 09:58.358
Hyeon Uk and Min Seok, you're both doing a great job.

189
09:58.358 --> 10:01.059
As for what happened yesterday...

190
10:01.059 --> 10:03.969
It's a mistake that could happen to anyone.

191
10:03.969 --> 10:06.773
Let's just do better from now on!

192
10:06.773 --> 10:09.555
I'll take better care of you, okay?

193
10:09.555 --> 10:11.543
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

194
10:13.198 --> 10:18.758
Sir, then about the disciplinary action or demerits...

195
10:18.758 --> 10:21.258
Why? Do you want to be punished?

196
10:21.258 --> 10:23.667
No, sir!

197
10:24.833 --> 10:28.218
The battalion commander didn't say much, so don't worry. It's okay.

198
10:28.218 --> 10:30.390
Oh... Is that so?

199
10:34.358 --> 10:35.678
Hyeon Uk.

200
10:35.678 --> 10:36.998
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

201
10:36.998 --> 10:39.208
How did it feel to fire a blank?

202
10:40.618 --> 10:41.848
Oh, well, that was...

203
10:41.848 --> 10:45.858
Since you fired a blank, why don't you fire a treat at the PX for Min Seok?

204
10:45.858 --> 10:47.278
Yes, sir.

205
10:47.278 --> 10:49.238
- Oh? Thank you! - Keep it under 2,000 won!

206
10:49.238 --> 10:51.778
He eats a lot.

207
10:51.778 --> 10:54.978
- Can't it be 20,000 won? - See? Look at him.

208
10:54.978 --> 10:58.547
- No, I'll buy it. - All right.

209
11:00.918 --> 11:03.378
Geez, Hyeon Uk.

210
11:03.378 --> 11:04.498
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

211
11:04.498 --> 11:08.118
It's okay. Relax and give us a smile!

212
11:08.118 --> 11:09.768
Let's see a smile.

213
11:12.088 --> 11:13.881
Hahaha. Laugh like this! Loudly!

214
11:13.881 --> 11:15.818
Hehe.

215
11:15.818 --> 11:19.542
- Oh, what am I going to do with him? - No, like this. Hahaha! Like a laugh exercise.

216
11:19.542 --> 11:20.789
Haha.

217
11:20.789 --> 11:24.155
Wait, wait. Hold on. Shh!

218
11:24.852 --> 11:26.344
Yes, First Sergeant.

219
11:27.055 --> 11:28.381
What?

220
11:30.273 --> 11:31.788
Chungseong! Love you!

221
11:31.788 --> 11:33.857
- You're here? - Yes.

222
11:47.666 --> 11:49.338
What's going on?

223
11:49.338 --> 11:51.287
Oh, man...

224
11:52.503 --> 11:53.678
Don't tell me...

225
11:53.678 --> 11:58.078
Responsibility starts at the top. The commander should take the blame.

226
11:58.078 --> 12:01.268
Wow... He's really something else.

227
12:02.398 --> 12:04.074
What's going on over there?

228
12:04.074 --> 12:06.874
Wow, I never thought I'd see a battalion commander doing full-gear laps.

229
12:06.874 --> 12:09.814
Man, it really must be time for me to discharge...

230
12:09.814 --> 12:11.461
I'm seeing all sorts of crazy things.

231
12:11.461 --> 12:13.394
He's telling everyone to stay on their toes.

232
12:13.394 --> 12:15.478
He says he'll take responsibility for mistakes.

233
12:15.478 --> 12:18.954
It's cool, but also a bit scary.

234
12:18.954 --> 12:21.825
Military life is about to get tough. Well, except for me.

235
12:21.825 --> 12:24.252
Wow, aren't you taking this too far?

236
12:30.834 --> 12:34.298
Responsibility starts at the top. The commander should take the blame.

237
12:34.298 --> 12:37.501
The commander... the commander...

238
12:45.854 --> 12:47.433
What do you think you're doing?

239
12:47.433 --> 12:51.334
Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin! As a platoon leader, I want to fulfill my responsibilities!

240
12:51.334 --> 12:54.374
Go back! This is my responsibility as the commander.

241
12:54.374 --> 12:55.914
Staying with the commander until the end...

242
12:55.914 --> 12:58.946
I believe that is the duty of a subordinate!

243
12:58.946 --> 13:02.365
You're so stubborn, choosing loyalty over orders.

244
13:02.365 --> 13:03.434
Now, go back.

245
13:03.434 --> 13:05.400
I shall continue on my path.

246
13:05.400 --> 13:07.063
Battalion Commander!

247
13:07.654 --> 13:09.755
Battalion Commander!

248
13:12.591 --> 13:14.614
Are you okay, sir?

249
13:14.614 --> 13:16.354
Why on earth...

250
13:16.354 --> 13:20.084
Why are you trying to bear all this alone?

251
13:20.968 --> 13:24.987
A commander must ultimately endure it alone.

252
13:24.987 --> 13:27.724
And that solitude is an officer's destiny.

253
13:27.724 --> 13:30.514
It's an officer's instinct.

254
13:30.514 --> 13:34.334
The immense responsibility and the weight of solitude you're carrying alone!

255
13:34.334 --> 13:38.074
I will share it now! No, I will carry it all!

256
13:38.074 --> 13:39.781
Give it to me!

257
13:40.474 --> 13:42.454
- What are you doing? - Please, give it to me!

258
13:42.454 --> 13:45.175
- Don't do this! - I'll carry it, sir!

259
13:49.814 --> 13:51.484
Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin!

260
13:53.114 --> 13:55.314
- Are you okay? - I'm fine, sir!

261
13:55.314 --> 13:58.588
- This won't do. Give me that gear! - I refuse, sir!

262
13:58.588 --> 14:01.754
This is an order, Oh Seok Jin. Give it here!

263
14:01.754 --> 14:03.574
I'm sorry, Battalion Commander.

264
14:03.574 --> 14:05.917
But this one order...

265
14:08.094 --> 14:09.794
I don't think I can follow it!

266
14:09.794 --> 14:13.094
Good heavens, man! You're going to ruin your knees!

267
14:13.094 --> 14:17.014
If I can support you, sir, I don't care if my knees break a hundred times!

268
14:17.014 --> 14:19.245
"These knees?"

269
14:22.514 --> 14:28.134
These knees are the pillars that will support the future of our country!

270
14:28.134 --> 14:31.294
No, sir! I'll carry it!

271
14:31.294 --> 14:35.264
The weight of this gear is the weight of responsibility!

272
14:38.434 --> 14:40.354
Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin...

273
14:40.354 --> 14:44.104
You are a true warrior.

274
14:48.534 --> 14:52.954
- Battalion Commander! - Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin! We go together now.

275
14:52.954 --> 14:54.474
Let's go.

276
14:54.474 --> 14:55.874
Battalion Commander!

277
14:55.874 --> 14:57.434
Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin.

278
14:57.434 --> 15:00.204
You're a true warrior.

279
15:02.374 --> 15:03.794
Battalion Commander!

280
15:03.794 --> 15:05.474
We'll join you too!

281
15:05.474 --> 15:06.697
- Give it to me! - No, sir!

282
15:06.697 --> 15:08.991
- It's an order. Give it to me! - Company Commander!

283
15:08.991 --> 15:12.037
- Master Sergeant Park Jae Su! Give it to me! - No, sir!

284
15:12.037 --> 15:14.608
- I'll carry it! - No, it's fine!

285
15:16.014 --> 15:19.114
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu! I'll carry it!

286
15:19.114 --> 15:21.570
Fine! You do it!

287
15:24.882 --> 15:28.556
Today, we have finally proven that we are one.

288
15:29.454 --> 15:33.944
You are all truly wonderful officers.

289
15:36.294 --> 15:37.754
Let's go together!

290
15:37.754 --> 15:40.474
- Yes, sir! - Good.

291
15:40.474 --> 15:43.634
Alright, forward march!

292
15:43.634 --> 15:46.084
One, two, three, four!

293
15:46.084 --> 15:47.667
- A cool! - A cool!

294
15:47.667 --> 15:49.323
- Man! - Man!

295
15:49.323 --> 15:54.294
There are many men, but I am the man!

296
15:54.294 --> 15:56.238
A cool man!

297
15:56.238 --> 15:59.464
Attention! Salute the commanders!

298
15:59.464 --> 16:02.425
- Chungseong! Love you! - Chungseong! Love you!

299
16:05.298 --> 16:09.428
The path the Battalion Commander walks... I shall walk it with him.

300
16:11.889 --> 16:15.851
Where is he going? He just went inside after mumbling to himself.

301
16:15.851 --> 16:18.937
But the Battalion Commander... He's not just all talk.

302
16:18.937 --> 16:22.290
I know. He surprises me every time.

303
16:29.514 --> 16:30.945
What's this?

304
16:32.434 --> 16:33.514
Is something wrong?

305
16:33.514 --> 16:34.734
Why are you in full gear?

306
16:34.734 --> 16:36.351
Where are you going in such a hurry?

307
16:36.351 --> 16:38.134
Oh, if you're looking for the Battalion Commander...

308
16:38.134 --> 16:39.594
He's already finished his run.

309
16:39.594 --> 16:41.262
Come again?

310
16:45.394 --> 16:47.064
Don't tell me you...

311
16:47.714 --> 16:50.474
- It's not like that. - Not like what?

312
16:50.474 --> 16:53.574
What exactly are you talking about, sir?

313
16:53.574 --> 16:56.808
You weren't planning to run alongside the Battalion Commander, were you?

314
16:56.808 --> 16:59.514
Absolutely not, sir...

315
16:59.514 --> 17:02.714
I'm just preparing for tomorrow's shooting practice in advance.

316
17:02.714 --> 17:05.094
Why do you need full gear for shooting?

317
17:05.094 --> 17:06.414
Train as you fight...

318
17:06.414 --> 17:09.114
It's to maintain a more perfect state of combat readiness.

319
17:09.114 --> 17:12.157
Then I'll go and get ready. Chungseong! Love you!

320
17:12.157 --> 17:13.793
Uh, sure.

321
17:17.746 --> 17:19.748
He's definitely trying to suck up.

322
17:19.748 --> 17:23.114
Seok Jin needs to suck up too. He shouldn't end up like me.

323
17:23.114 --> 17:25.105
Will that even work?

324
17:32.054 --> 17:35.754
- Oh, right! Did you hear the news? - What news?

325
17:35.754 --> 17:39.309
I heard the current and former Battalion Commanders met up.

326
17:39.309 --> 17:41.144
With the... former Battalion Commander?

327
17:41.144 --> 17:45.482
Yeah. Seong Min said he saw them at the cafe out front.

328
17:45.482 --> 17:48.333
Do you know why they met?

329
17:48.333 --> 17:50.987
I'm not sure about that...

330
17:50.987 --> 17:55.534
They're alumni from the same school, so maybe they just met up.

331
17:55.534 --> 17:57.494
That's possible.

332
17:57.494 --> 17:59.664
I doubt anything good was discussed.

333
18:02.416 --> 18:04.802
It's probably nothing.

334
18:08.213 --> 18:10.218
Corporal Park Min Seok, what kind of...

335
18:10.218 --> 18:14.308
Oh, thanks for the apple.

336
18:15.387 --> 18:17.560
- Sit down. - Yes, sir.

337
18:20.517 --> 18:26.138
Corporal Park Min Seok... I'm really sorry about yesterday.

338
18:26.138 --> 18:30.798
No, it's okay. I should have supervised you better.

339
18:30.798 --> 18:34.738
But I'm glad everything was resolved smoothly. Right?

340
18:34.738 --> 18:36.188
Usually, when this happens,

341
18:36.188 --> 18:40.998
you get demerits or even lose all your vacation days.

342
18:40.998 --> 18:45.108
I think they let it slide because we both have good records.

343
18:45.938 --> 18:47.398
Did you see how he ran with such discipline until the end?

344
18:47.398 --> 18:50.938
He must have great stamina. I bet he doesn't even smoke.

345
18:50.938 --> 18:52.314
Oh my, Park Min Seok.

346
18:52.314 --> 18:53.440
Corporal Park Min Seok.

347
18:53.440 --> 18:54.546
How did it go?

348
18:54.546 --> 18:57.118
He just told me to be more careful next time.

349
18:57.118 --> 19:00.638
Man, being the division commander's son has its perks. He just let it go.

350
19:00.638 --> 19:02.318
No, it's not like that.

351
19:02.318 --> 19:04.418
Like hell it isn't. The battalion commander was running laps for you.

352
19:04.418 --> 19:08.158
Yeah, I saw that too. I was so surprised.

353
19:08.158 --> 19:11.328
Corporal Park Min Seok? Do you have a moment?

354
19:11.328 --> 19:13.888
Se Gye, what's up? Is something wrong?

355
19:15.978 --> 19:20.088
Well, it's about Hyeon Uk.

356
19:21.418 --> 19:23.038
Is he really okay?

357
19:23.038 --> 19:26.398
Huh? All of a sudden? In what way?

358
19:26.398 --> 19:30.544
Well, last time...

359
19:30.544 --> 19:32.703
When I saw him in the bathroom,

360
19:32.703 --> 19:36.759
he was acting strange after eating ramen, and...

361
19:36.759 --> 19:41.055
When there was a fuss about the night watch, I definitely went to wake him up.

362
19:41.055 --> 19:45.138
But it felt like he didn't wake me up on purpose.

363
19:45.138 --> 19:49.478
I'm not sure if he's just struggling to adjust or if something else is up.

364
19:49.478 --> 19:53.438
Since you know him well, Corporal Park, I wanted to ask you about it.

365
19:53.438 --> 19:55.638
Oh, that happened?

366
19:55.638 --> 20:00.242
I might just be oversensitive, but I wanted to mention it just in case.

367
20:00.242 --> 20:03.829
If it's nothing, then don't worry about it.

368
20:03.829 --> 20:07.238
He's probably just nervous. I was like that all the time as a private.

369
20:07.238 --> 20:09.158
He just got here, after all.

370
20:09.898 --> 20:12.848
Still, you're the only one looking out for your junior.

371
20:12.848 --> 20:15.978
- It's nothing. - Thanks for caring. Let's go.

372
20:15.978 --> 20:17.408
Yes, sir!

373
20:18.277 --> 20:21.125
Private Kim Hyeon Uk! I've never seen such a top-tier ace like you.

374
20:21.125 --> 20:23.058
- Thank you! - He's on a different level than Ji Jeong Min.

375
20:23.058 --> 20:25.398
- Hey, I used to be an ace too. - What do you mean, "used to be?"

376
20:25.398 --> 20:28.618
Look at him. He's adjusting just fine.

377
20:28.618 --> 20:30.600
Yes, he is.

378
20:32.138 --> 20:34.034
- Let's go. - Yes, sir!

379
20:40.018 --> 20:41.678
- Did you finish your smoke? - Yes, sir.

380
20:41.678 --> 20:43.221
Let's head inside.

381
20:43.911 --> 20:45.441
Keep up the good work.

382
20:58.535 --> 21:00.678
Attention, announcement from the officer on duty.

383
21:00.678 --> 21:03.418
Get the keys to the gun rack now and begin cleaning your firearms.

384
21:03.418 --> 21:05.528
Two minutes left.

385
21:06.888 --> 21:07.738
Repeating.

386
21:07.738 --> 21:11.478
In two minutes, get the keys to the gun rack and clean your firearms. That is all.

387
21:11.478 --> 21:14.318
- Hey, Assistant Platoon Leader! Look at this. - What?

388
21:14.318 --> 21:16.687
The views on your photo are insane, sir.

389
21:16.687 --> 21:18.398
Huh? My photo? Why?

390
21:18.398 --> 21:21.010
I only had eight views before. How did this happen?

391
21:21.010 --> 21:22.406
Let me see.

392
21:22.406 --> 21:24.451
[Sergeant First Class Im Seong Min: 730 Views] Huh? It's true.

393
21:24.451 --> 21:27.447
Did you manipulate this yourself?

394
21:27.447 --> 21:30.486
Hey, why would I? Is it a glitch?

395
21:30.486 --> 21:33.083
- You can open it now. - Oh, okay.

396
21:33.083 --> 21:35.158
Platoon Leader, sir.

397
21:35.158 --> 21:37.816
It starts at 7:40. Didn't you get the word?

398
21:37.816 --> 21:41.318
Jeez. Is someone stalking me?

399
21:48.718 --> 21:51.175
He's really handsome.

400
21:51.810 --> 21:57.036
You're such a cool soldier.

401
21:57.036 --> 22:00.209
Keep it up!

402
22:04.438 --> 22:08.478
Wait, this is...

403
22:08.478 --> 22:11.578
Thanks for the tissues last time.

404
22:11.578 --> 22:14.078
Carry this with you.

405
22:14.078 --> 22:16.602
Chungseong. Love you.

406
22:43.418 --> 22:44.698
- Hyeon Uk! - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

407
22:44.698 --> 22:46.868
- Come over here. - Yes, sir.

408
22:47.958 --> 22:52.658
Don't cut the cleaning patch too thick. Just about this much? A finger's width?

409
22:52.658 --> 22:56.333
Cut it like this and look at the cleaning rod. See the slot here?

410
22:56.333 --> 22:57.723
Yes, I see it.

411
22:57.723 --> 22:59.588
Slide it in here like this.

412
22:59.588 --> 23:02.973
If you do it too hard or too fast, it might get stuck.

413
23:02.973 --> 23:04.878
- See the charging handle? - Yes, I see it.

414
23:04.878 --> 23:07.593
Just clean up to the charging handle.

415
23:07.593 --> 23:09.178
Yes, sir.

416
23:09.178 --> 23:12.278
The battalion commander said to clean the bolt carrier group today, so keep it in mind.

417
23:12.278 --> 23:13.778
Yes, sir.

418
23:13.778 --> 23:16.898
- The bolt carrier group? - Haven't you disassembled it before?

419
23:16.898 --> 23:20.698
Well, I have, but it's been a while...

420
23:20.698 --> 23:24.218
- Im Da Hye, what about you? - I'm sorry, sir.

421
23:24.218 --> 23:27.818
Jeez, you guys are corporals. Where did all your experience go?

422
23:27.818 --> 23:29.241
Look closely.

423
23:29.241 --> 23:31.243
- Hey, Bit Na Ri. - Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri.

424
23:31.243 --> 23:33.704
- What's this? - It's the firing pin.

425
23:33.704 --> 23:38.258
Right. You know you'll go to the brig if you lose this, right?

426
23:38.258 --> 23:41.418
When this firing pin strikes the primer,

427
23:41.418 --> 23:44.478
the gunpowder explodes and the bullet is fired.

428
23:44.478 --> 23:48.568
But do you know what's more important than the firing pin?

429
23:49.219 --> 23:52.669
It's this. The firing pin retaining pin.

430
23:52.669 --> 23:54.810
If you lose this, you're in big trouble.

431
23:54.810 --> 23:57.688
The gun won't fire, or it'll jam while firing.

432
23:57.688 --> 24:01.158
If you're really unlucky, the barrel will explode.

433
24:01.158 --> 24:02.734
You have to take good care of it. Got it?

434
24:02.734 --> 24:04.358
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

435
24:04.358 --> 24:06.459
Okay. Everyone, disassemble the bolt carrier.

436
24:06.459 --> 24:08.009
Yes, sir.

437
24:10.951 --> 24:13.313
- You try it too. - Yes, sir.

438
24:13.313 --> 24:14.574
Sergeant Kim Sang Hun.

439
24:14.574 --> 24:16.927
- Yeah, what? - I can't find the retaining pin.

440
24:16.927 --> 24:19.712
Sigh, how much more do I have to teach you?

441
24:20.376 --> 24:21.854
Mine is defective.

442
24:21.854 --> 24:24.460
What do you mean defective, man?

443
24:26.254 --> 24:28.974
Man, when are we going to get up to the shooting range?

444
24:28.974 --> 24:31.034
Is this right for someone about to discharge?

445
24:31.034 --> 24:32.884
Hey, let's take a break.

446
24:32.884 --> 24:34.059
Take a break.

447
24:34.059 --> 24:35.590
- Break! - Break!

448
24:35.590 --> 24:38.187
Hey, be quiet and get in line. I want to take a picture.

449
24:38.187 --> 24:39.834
- Get in line. - Get in line.

450
24:39.834 --> 24:42.191
What, are you a photographer now?

451
24:42.191 --> 24:44.394
Knock it off. I'm already annoyed as it is.

452
24:44.394 --> 24:46.987
Not a photographer, but a photo sergeant?

453
24:46.987 --> 24:49.004
Or maybe a photo snapper?

454
24:49.774 --> 24:52.491
Wow, you guys in your final months sure have a way with words.

455
24:52.491 --> 24:56.000
- Shut it before I take your funeral photo. - Yes, sir!

456
25:00.994 --> 25:03.714
Hey, you soldiers, don't be so camera-conscious.

457
25:03.714 --> 25:07.064
Especially Im Da Hye. Put that thumb down.

458
25:07.064 --> 25:07.777
I'm sorry!

459
25:07.777 --> 25:10.974
I'll take solo shots at the range, so let's keep it up!

460
25:10.974 --> 25:12.074
Yes, sir!

461
25:12.074 --> 25:15.054
We're almost at the shooting range, so let's push through.

462
25:15.054 --> 25:17.334
And since there was an accidental discharge of blanks earlier,

463
25:17.334 --> 25:20.602
everyone stay focused during training, understand?

464
25:20.602 --> 25:21.874
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

465
25:21.874 --> 25:23.542
- Let's move out. - Moving out!

466
25:23.542 --> 25:25.470
- Moving out! - Moving out!

467
25:26.294 --> 25:28.434
Good, good.

468
25:28.434 --> 25:32.194
Those bastards in the admin office are lucky. No shooting, no training.

469
25:32.194 --> 25:37.484
Exactly. They have it so easy. Total slackers.

470
25:44.127 --> 25:46.188
Oh, Sergeant Major! Chungseong! Love you!

471
25:46.188 --> 25:48.314
Mrrgh... mmph... mnnh...

472
25:48.314 --> 25:50.676
Huh? Come again?

473
25:50.676 --> 25:53.802
- Mrrgh! - Corporal Sung Yoon Mo!

474
25:53.802 --> 25:57.985
Uh, Jumoni Sapsirengdeun... uh...

475
25:57.985 --> 26:01.018
Did you say Jumoni Sapsirengdeun?

476
26:01.018 --> 26:05.065
Yeah! Jumoni Sapsirengdeun, Eum-yu-si-in Jurassic Dapeokeo.

477
26:05.065 --> 26:09.526
Eum-yu-si-in Jurassic Dapeokeo?

478
26:09.526 --> 26:13.117
What the hell is he saying?

479
26:13.117 --> 26:16.544
Ullala Jeollala...

480
26:16.544 --> 26:20.952
Gaesibal Bucheonima...

481
26:20.952 --> 26:23.030
Yes... I understand.

482
26:26.584 --> 26:28.045
I'm screwed.

483
26:28.045 --> 26:30.062
I didn't understand a single word...

484
26:30.062 --> 26:34.723
Oh, man. What do I do...

485
26:34.723 --> 26:36.914
I'll write it down while I remember.

486
26:36.914 --> 26:40.277
"Jumoni Sapsirengdeun..."

487
26:42.226 --> 26:49.874
"Jumoni Sapsirengdeun, Eum-yu-si-in Jurassic Dapeokeo, Gaesibal."

488
26:49.874 --> 26:51.454
Hey, what are you doing?

489
26:51.454 --> 26:54.334
- Corporal No Hee Jeong, we're in trouble. - What did you mess up? Again?

490
26:54.334 --> 26:58.285
No, it's not that. While you were out sweeping leaves, Corporal,

491
26:58.285 --> 27:00.777
the Sergeant Major came by and...

492
27:00.777 --> 27:02.495
Just spit it out, man!

493
27:02.495 --> 27:06.734
He told me to do something, but I...

494
27:06.734 --> 27:08.794
I couldn't understand a single word.

495
27:08.794 --> 27:12.854
- So I wrote down what I remembered. - What is it? Let me see!

496
27:12.854 --> 27:18.074
"Jumoni Sapsirengdeun, Eum-yu-si-in Jurassic Dapeokeo, Gaesibal Bucheonima?"

497
27:18.074 --> 27:20.234
Do you want to die?

498
27:20.234 --> 27:22.554
That's really what he said.

499
27:22.554 --> 27:25.754
Damn it. Let's try to decipher this first.

500
27:25.754 --> 27:27.771
Let's start with "Jumoni Sapsirengdeun."

501
27:27.771 --> 27:31.504
Jumoni Sapsirengdeun...

502
27:31.504 --> 27:35.155
Jumoni Sapsirengdeun...

503
27:35.155 --> 27:39.334
- Juim-wonsasil-e inneun! - In the Sergeant Major's office!

504
27:39.334 --> 27:41.994
- Oh, I think that's it! - That's it! That's it!

505
27:41.994 --> 27:43.994
Okay, let's try "Eum-yu-si-in Jurassic."

506
27:43.994 --> 27:48.834
Eum-yu-si-in Jurassic, Eum-yu-si-in... Eum-si-in, Eum-sin, Eum-sing, Eumsik!

507
27:48.834 --> 27:52.234
- Food waste! - I think it's food waste!

508
27:52.234 --> 27:54.174
Wow, Corporal No Hee Jeong, you're a genius.

509
27:54.174 --> 27:56.794
How did you hear "food waste" as "Eum-yu-si-in Jurassic?"

510
27:56.794 --> 27:58.594
Should I spray WD-40 in your ears?

511
27:58.594 --> 28:00.234
But that's really what it sounded like.

512
28:00.234 --> 28:03.772
Okay, look! We got "food waste in the Sergeant Major's office," right?

513
28:03.772 --> 28:06.274
- Yes, sir. - Now, what's next? Then!

514
28:06.274 --> 28:08.554
"Da-peokeo Gaesibal Bucheonima." What the hell is this?

515
28:08.554 --> 28:10.230
Da-peokeo Gaesibal Bucheonima...

516
28:10.230 --> 28:13.735
Chungseong! Sergeant Major!

517
28:13.735 --> 28:16.794
By any chance, is there food waste in the Sergeant Major's office?

518
28:16.794 --> 28:19.686
Yeah, Eum-yu-si-in Jurassic.

519
28:21.414 --> 28:24.234
May I ask if we're supposed to scoop it all up and eat it?

520
28:24.234 --> 28:26.323
Huh? Ehh?

521
28:26.323 --> 28:29.708
I mean, scooping up all that food waste and just going like...

522
28:29.708 --> 28:33.494
No, no, that's not it. How could anyone eat that...

523
28:33.494 --> 28:36.840
- I beg your pardon! - What's going on? First Sergeant?

524
28:36.840 --> 28:41.680
It's just that it's so hard to understand the Sergeant Major.

525
28:42.324 --> 28:46.672
Sir, please calm down and tell me what you said.

526
28:47.414 --> 28:49.049
You punks!

527
28:50.034 --> 28:53.117
When did I tell you to eat food waste?

528
28:55.110 --> 28:57.587
I said pour out all the food waste in the Sergeant Major's office!

529
28:57.587 --> 29:01.772
Oh! "Jumoni Sapsirengdeun Eum-yu-si-in Jurassic Da-peokeo!"

530
29:03.700 --> 29:06.119
And I told you to wash the sink floor mats clean!

531
29:06.119 --> 29:08.916
- Oh! "Gaesibal Bucheonima!" - Oh! "Gaesibal Bucheonima!"

532
29:09.831 --> 29:12.542
Why can't you do your job right? Huh? Do I look like a joke to you?

533
29:12.542 --> 29:14.194
No, it's not that...

534
29:15.672 --> 29:17.158
Is the Sergeant Major a joke?

535
29:17.158 --> 29:18.948
- Huh? What? - Huh? What?

536
29:18.948 --> 29:20.554
I beg your pardon?

537
29:21.803 --> 29:24.594
Oh... not a joke, but you're the eldest son?

538
29:24.594 --> 29:27.513
- Oh, so you're the eldest son. - Oh, so you're the eldest son.

539
29:28.628 --> 29:33.991
Huh? Argh... Fucking hell!

540
29:34.754 --> 29:36.394
Hey, did he just say "fucking hell?"

541
29:36.394 --> 29:38.614
He definitely said "fucking hell."

542
29:38.614 --> 29:41.254
Sir, do you know what "fucking hell" means?

543
29:41.254 --> 29:44.154
If the First Sergeant can't understand him, how are we supposed to?

544
29:44.154 --> 29:47.714
That's the first time I've seen the First Sergeant get hit.

545
29:47.714 --> 29:49.214
Do you want to get hit too, then?

546
29:49.214 --> 29:51.124
- What? - Come here.

547
29:53.794 --> 29:57.834
It's because of you! Because you don't listen properly!

548
29:57.834 --> 30:00.465
- Everyone, focus! - Focus!

549
30:00.465 --> 30:05.594
Since we're using live ammo, stay focused during the drill.

550
30:05.594 --> 30:06.994
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

551
30:06.994 --> 30:09.254
Ji Jeong Min, don't doze off!

552
30:09.254 --> 30:11.143
- I'm sorry, sir! - Get your head in the game!

553
30:11.143 --> 30:12.154
I'm sorry, sir!

554
30:12.154 --> 30:15.394
- Team 3! Receive magazines! - Receive magazines!

555
30:15.394 --> 30:16.842
Corporal Cha Byeong Ho.

556
30:16.842 --> 30:18.662
- Check magazines! - Check magazines!

557
30:18.662 --> 30:21.082
- Nine rounds, top-left, all clear! - Nine rounds, top-left, all clear!

558
30:21.082 --> 30:24.590
- Shooters, prone position! - Prone position!

559
30:26.302 --> 30:28.982
- Hand over magazines! - Hand over magazines!

560
30:28.982 --> 30:30.411
- Nine rounds, top-left, all clear! - Nine rounds, top-left, all clear!

561
30:30.411 --> 30:33.492
- Insert magazines! - Insert magazines!

562
30:34.342 --> 30:37.082
- Bolt forward! - Bolt forward!

563
30:37.082 --> 30:39.562
- Selector to semi! - Selector to semi!

564
30:39.562 --> 30:44.552
- Ready shooters, commence firing! - Commence firing!

565
30:49.264 --> 30:51.351
Wow, he's a good shot.

566
30:53.685 --> 30:55.939
Moon Bit Na Ri, nice!

567
30:59.842 --> 31:01.472
Commence firing!

568
31:03.445 --> 31:06.907
- Uh... Platoon Leader, my rifle won't fire. - No, no!

569
31:06.907 --> 31:09.034
- Keep the rifle still! - Where are you looking? Look ahead!

570
31:09.034 --> 31:10.162
- Just raise your right arm. - Yes, sir!

571
31:10.162 --> 31:13.207
No, your right leg, right leg!

572
31:13.207 --> 31:15.401
Malfunction! Malfunction!

573
31:15.401 --> 31:18.043
- Cease fire! - Cease fire!

574
31:18.043 --> 31:21.922
- Park Min Seok, don't move! - Yes, sir!

575
31:21.922 --> 31:24.442
Lane 4, put down your rifle and kneel.

576
31:24.442 --> 31:27.832
- Put down your rifle and kneel. - Put down your rifle and kneel.

577
31:27.832 --> 31:29.582
All lanes, resume firing!

578
31:29.582 --> 31:31.016
- Resume firing. - Resume firing.

579
31:31.016 --> 31:32.222
Selector to semi.

580
31:32.222 --> 31:33.822
Hey, Seok Jin, what's the matter?

581
31:33.822 --> 31:37.482
Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin. It's a malfunction, but I haven't found the cause.

582
31:37.482 --> 31:39.122
I'll check it as soon as the firing is over.

583
31:39.122 --> 31:42.695
- Lane 2, finished firing! - Lane 2, finished firing!

584
31:48.162 --> 31:50.644
Nothing seems wrong, but...

585
31:52.454 --> 31:53.870
Huh?

586
31:53.870 --> 31:56.462
Hey, why is this missing?

587
31:56.462 --> 31:57.780
What is it, sir?

588
31:57.780 --> 32:01.004
The firing pin retaining pin is gone.

589
32:01.004 --> 32:02.182
Hey, Park Min Seok!

590
32:02.182 --> 32:06.682
- No, sir. I... what happened? - Did it fall out while cleaning?

591
32:06.682 --> 32:11.142
- No, sir. I definitely put it in... - That could've been a disaster.

592
32:11.142 --> 32:12.942
Man, that was close.

593
32:12.942 --> 32:16.142
I told you so many times. Get your head in the game!

594
32:16.142 --> 32:19.742
But I really, really put it in, sir.

595
32:19.742 --> 32:22.342
- That's really strange. - Hey, Park Min Seok.

596
32:22.342 --> 32:24.542
- Corporal Park Min Seok. - Are you sure you did it right?

597
32:24.542 --> 32:27.182
Yes, I'm sure I put it in.

598
32:27.182 --> 32:29.533
- I'm sorry. - This is unbelievable.

599
32:29.533 --> 32:31.762
Did you use it as a toothpick after eating or something?

600
32:31.762 --> 32:34.902
No, sir. I'm positive I put it in.

601
32:34.902 --> 32:36.413
Be quiet.

602
32:42.642 --> 32:45.172
Trainee number 11, Kim Hyeon Uk.

603
32:47.605 --> 32:51.986
[11 months ago, 95th Division Training Camp]

604
32:51.986 --> 32:56.663
Trainee Kim Hyeon Uk, you are hereby dismissed.

605
33:06.776 --> 33:09.964
[Certificate of Discharge]

606
33:14.902 --> 33:16.565
Park Min Seok...

607
33:17.525 --> 33:19.409
It's all your fault.

608
33:29.302 --> 33:31.402
- Hyeon Uk. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

609
33:31.402 --> 33:36.662
For things like this, the top is plastic and the bottom is vinyl, so separate them.

610
33:36.662 --> 33:39.282
- Yes, sir. - Finish up the paper over here.

611
33:39.282 --> 33:41.536
- I'll finish up here. - Yes, sir!

612
33:59.037 --> 34:00.938
It's over! Good work, Hyeon Uk.

613
34:00.938 --> 34:02.842
You worked hard too, PFC Moon Bit Na Ri.

614
34:02.842 --> 34:05.931
Let's head back later. If we go in now, we'll just have to work more.

615
34:05.931 --> 34:08.022
Then, would it be okay if I go wash my hands first?

616
34:08.022 --> 34:10.483
Sure, go ahead. I'll finish this up.

617
34:10.483 --> 34:11.839
Thank you!

618
34:12.962 --> 34:14.972
Did you finish what I told you to do?

619
34:16.724 --> 34:18.002
Oh, I thought the deadline was today.

620
34:18.002 --> 34:22.143
If it's due today, you should've finished by now! You're getting slack.

621
34:23.382 --> 34:28.262
Park Min Seok, you've been quiet since becoming a corporal, but now this?

622
34:28.262 --> 34:30.946
What else would you expect from a dummy like Min Seok?

623
34:30.946 --> 34:34.241
But I really did assemble it correctly.

624
34:34.241 --> 34:37.222
Did it grow legs and walk away if it was assembled so well?

625
34:37.222 --> 34:41.096
- It's true, Deputy Platoon Leader. - Like hell it is. Just write the report.

626
34:42.402 --> 34:46.842
You cause such a variety of trouble. I should be scolding Kim Sang Hun.

627
34:46.842 --> 34:48.562
I'm telling the truth, sir!

628
34:48.562 --> 34:51.502
Stop making excuses and write it if you don't want to die!

629
34:51.502 --> 34:54.935
- I'm sorry. - You must want to die. You're crazy.

630
34:56.219 --> 34:57.694
What's all the noise about?

631
34:57.694 --> 35:00.462
- Chungseong! Love you. - Love? You almost got shot.

632
35:00.462 --> 35:02.512
- Hey, Park Min Seok. - Corporal Park Min Seok.

633
35:02.512 --> 35:05.022
You're lucky nothing happened. If there had been an accident...

634
35:05.022 --> 35:07.742
the Company Commander and Battalion Commander would've been fired. Got it?

635
35:07.742 --> 35:10.452
Especially at such a critical time...

636
35:10.452 --> 35:11.562
I'm sorry.

637
35:11.562 --> 35:14.523
Whether your leave is canceled, or you go to disciplinary camp or the brig...

638
35:14.523 --> 35:16.481
Well, we'll just have to see.

639
35:20.123 --> 35:23.382
- Did you write it? - Well, this is...

640
35:23.382 --> 35:24.642
Where are you going?

641
35:24.642 --> 35:27.221
- Just to the bathroom. - Sit down, you bastard!

642
35:27.902 --> 35:29.762
How dare you try to go to the bathroom in this situation?

643
35:29.762 --> 35:33.655
- Get it together, will you? - I gave the order...

644
35:33.655 --> 35:37.250
- Get it together! - Oh, man.

645
35:37.250 --> 35:39.787
[I truly apologize for it]

646
35:44.392 --> 35:48.422
Huh? Is this... a firing pin retaining pin?

647
35:48.422 --> 35:50.197
PFC Moon Bit Na Ri?

648
35:51.422 --> 35:53.062
Shouldn't we be heading back now?

649
35:53.062 --> 35:54.862
No, my stomach suddenly hurts.

650
35:54.862 --> 35:57.322
I'll go to the bathroom and then buy something tasty at the PX.

651
35:57.322 --> 35:58.922
Yes, sir.

652
36:03.782 --> 36:08.512
Whether your leave is canceled, or you go to disciplinary camp or the brig...

653
36:10.003 --> 36:11.861
Corporal Park Min Seok?

654
36:12.670 --> 36:14.310
Can I talk to you for a second?

655
36:14.310 --> 36:17.419
Talk? Why?

656
36:19.742 --> 36:21.094
Why?

657
36:25.642 --> 36:29.374
Is this the firing pin retaining pin?

658
36:29.374 --> 36:32.834
- Where did you get this? - I found it at the recycling center.

659
36:32.834 --> 36:35.594
The recycling center? Who threw it away?

660
36:35.594 --> 36:37.407
I'm not sure about that.

661
36:38.194 --> 36:39.494
Who did you go with?

662
36:39.494 --> 36:42.424
I went with Hyeon Uk.

663
36:43.114 --> 36:47.794
I think he was throwing something away, but I'm not sure if this was it.

664
36:47.794 --> 36:53.114
I was sorting the plastics, and when Hyeon Uk went to wash his hands...

665
36:53.114 --> 36:54.834
Corporal Park Min Seok!

666
37:01.634 --> 37:04.090
Se Gye, have you seen Kim Hyeon Uk?

667
37:04.090 --> 37:05.851
Private Jeon Se Gye!

668
37:05.851 --> 37:08.568
I saw Hyeon Uk at the drying area.

669
37:22.754 --> 37:25.354
- Kim Hyeon Uk. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

670
37:25.354 --> 37:26.854
What is it?

671
37:27.454 --> 37:29.014
It was you, right?

672
37:29.014 --> 37:30.944
What are you talking about?

673
37:36.632 --> 37:38.392
What? Why is that there?

674
37:40.994 --> 37:43.004
Why is that there?

675
37:43.934 --> 37:45.674
Are you crazy?

676
37:45.674 --> 37:47.904
I said, are you crazy?

677
37:47.904 --> 37:50.292
Do you know how dangerous it is if this goes missing?

678
37:50.292 --> 37:51.474
Why did you do it?

679
37:51.474 --> 37:53.964
You bastard! Why did you do it?

680
37:55.874 --> 37:57.755
You're asking me why?

681
38:03.114 --> 38:05.577
Corporal Park Min Seok?

682
38:08.154 --> 38:13.704
Corporal Im Da Hye told me to bring Private Kim Hyeon Uk right away.

683
38:14.634 --> 38:18.384
- Go on, then. - Yes, sir! Keep up the good work!

684
38:31.234 --> 38:32.874
You didn't doze off, did you?

685
38:32.874 --> 38:34.857
No, I didn't. I just got the time wrong.

686
38:34.857 --> 38:38.110
I came to wake him up, but it felt like he didn't wake me up on purpose.

687
38:38.110 --> 38:40.294
I should've kept a better lookout earlier. I'm sorry.

688
38:40.294 --> 38:41.554
I'm really sorry.

689
38:41.554 --> 38:44.764
Corporal Park Min Seok, I'm sorry. It's all because of me...

690
38:46.094 --> 38:47.775
What? Why is that there?

691
38:50.934 --> 38:54.834
Corporal Park Min Seok, are you okay?

692
38:54.834 --> 38:57.827
Oh, it's nothing.

693
39:00.296 --> 39:04.428
- Se Gye, keep at it. I'll head out first. - Yes, sir.

694
39:11.974 --> 39:14.634
Whoa! It's overflowing! It's overflowing!

695
39:14.634 --> 39:16.036
Sorry.

696
39:17.574 --> 39:21.320
No, it's okay. I actually prefer bland food anyway.

697
39:21.320 --> 39:22.494
Should I do that for you?

698
39:22.494 --> 39:24.746
- I'll do it. - Yes, sir.

699
39:29.294 --> 39:30.775
Yes, sir.

700
39:32.161 --> 39:34.394
Corporal Im Da Hye, what kind of food do you usually like?

701
39:34.394 --> 39:37.683
I like cream udon and Schnell Chicken.

702
39:44.500 --> 39:47.800
[Ministry of National Defense] [Barracks Reform 2.0]

703
39:50.918 --> 39:53.929
[Rewards for the Best-Performing Unit]

704
39:55.894 --> 39:58.273
Yes, this is Lieutenant Colonel Byeon Hyeok Jin.

705
39:58.273 --> 40:03.987
Chungseong! Yes, I understand exactly what you mean.

706
40:03.987 --> 40:05.995
Yes, but...

707
40:06.814 --> 40:08.234
No, sir.

708
40:08.234 --> 40:10.864
[Promotion Priority for Commanders of Selected Units] I'll reorganize it and report back tomorrow.

709
40:10.864 --> 40:13.504
Good work, sir. Chungseong!

710
40:20.094 --> 40:22.034
Byeon, everything's been okay, right?

711
40:22.034 --> 40:24.674
Yes, I've been doing well.

712
40:24.674 --> 40:28.014
Sir, I heard you've been transferred to the Army Headquarters.

713
40:28.014 --> 40:29.614
It's a bit late, but congratulations.

714
40:29.614 --> 40:34.174
I thought I'd be forced to retire soon as a policy researcher at HQ.

715
40:34.174 --> 40:38.836
Oh, you might know this. Major General Kim Seung Hye, whom I've served...

716
40:38.836 --> 40:43.068
since I was a rookie platoon leader, is now the Director of Personnel at HQ.

717
40:43.068 --> 40:47.894
He told me I can look forward to what's next, so I'm hopeful.

718
40:47.894 --> 40:51.374
Sir, I'm sure there will be good news.

719
40:51.374 --> 40:54.838
Well, we'll have to wait and see.

720
40:57.499 --> 40:59.365
How is the 2nd Company Commander?

721
40:59.365 --> 41:02.754
Are you talking about Captain Cho Baek Ho?

722
41:02.754 --> 41:05.194
He's doing well, sir.

723
41:05.194 --> 41:09.134
This is his last chance for a promotion, right?

724
41:09.134 --> 41:11.774
Yes, that's what I understand.

725
41:11.774 --> 41:14.284
What do you think of him?

726
41:17.634 --> 41:19.674
What do you mean, sir?

727
41:19.674 --> 41:23.775
Would a soldier like Captain Cho Baek Ho be an asset to the organization...

728
41:23.775 --> 41:26.075
or a liability if he stays?

729
41:36.538 --> 41:42.214
We need your active support to be chosen as a Barracks Reform 2.0 pilot unit.

730
41:42.214 --> 41:45.130
Support? We will follow your orders, sir!

731
41:45.130 --> 41:47.594
That's right. You don't have to worry!

732
41:47.594 --> 41:50.094
Do you think I'm doing this for my own benefit?

733
41:50.094 --> 41:52.588
It's for the soldiers and for you.

734
41:52.588 --> 41:54.864
- That's right! - Of course!

735
41:57.794 --> 41:59.544
Isn't that right?

736
42:01.438 --> 42:03.214
Yes, sir. That's right.

737
42:04.014 --> 42:07.774
Sudden changes can confuse the soldiers,

738
42:07.774 --> 42:11.674
so I'd like the company commanders to handle them well.

739
42:11.674 --> 42:13.274
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

740
42:21.748 --> 42:23.836
- Shall we sit down? - Yes, sir.

741
42:26.754 --> 42:31.389
Gosh, this is nice.

742
42:32.246 --> 42:35.866
I haven't been in the army for long,

743
42:35.866 --> 42:38.606
but you're quite special, Captain Cho.

744
42:38.606 --> 42:39.935
Me, sir?

745
42:39.935 --> 42:42.546
The way you care for your soldiers.

746
42:42.546 --> 42:47.025
- It's not that special, sir. - No, it is special.

747
42:47.025 --> 42:52.310
Taking new recruits to the bathhouse and singing for them during roll call...

748
42:52.310 --> 42:54.406
I'm sure the soldiers really love it.

749
42:54.406 --> 43:00.346
I just do what I can, but... How did you know all that?

750
43:00.346 --> 43:03.076
I just did a little research.

751
43:04.126 --> 43:07.227
I'm learning a lot from you, Captain Cho.

752
43:07.227 --> 43:09.012
No, sir.

753
43:10.546 --> 43:13.866
Remember what I said earlier?

754
43:13.866 --> 43:17.963
- Yes. - You're reluctant because of the soldiers?

755
43:17.963 --> 43:20.606
- No, sir. - Really?

756
43:20.606 --> 43:22.866
You looked like you thought this was too hasty.

757
43:22.866 --> 43:25.453
Like we're just pushing ahead without asking the soldiers...

758
43:25.453 --> 43:29.127
or caring about their intentions. That's what your face said.

759
43:30.323 --> 43:32.332
Was I right?

760
43:33.226 --> 43:36.156
I can't say you're wrong, sir.

761
43:38.932 --> 43:40.351
Just as I heard.

762
43:40.351 --> 43:41.746
I'm sorry, sir.

763
43:41.746 --> 43:44.206
No, there's nothing to be sorry about.

764
43:44.206 --> 43:48.000
It would be nice if the military had such processes,

765
43:48.000 --> 43:51.684
but I think it runs because it doesn't have them.

766
43:52.386 --> 43:55.276
Yes, sir. I understand what you mean.

767
43:55.866 --> 44:00.328
Well... what you see isn't everything, so don't hate me too much.

768
44:00.328 --> 44:02.390
Hate you? Absolutely not, sir.

769
44:02.390 --> 44:03.604
Oh, really?

770
44:03.604 --> 44:08.326
Your face says, "Why is a guy who loves showing off suddenly saying this?"

771
44:08.326 --> 44:09.886
Am I right about this too?

772
44:09.886 --> 44:12.838
No, sir. How could I...

773
44:13.706 --> 44:15.626
You're up for promotion review this time, right?

774
44:15.626 --> 44:17.546
Yes, sir.

775
44:17.546 --> 44:19.206
It's your last chance, right?

776
44:19.206 --> 44:23.705
Yes. If I don't get promoted this time, I'll likely...

777
44:23.705 --> 44:26.033
have to take off my uniform.

778
44:29.807 --> 44:31.926
Battalion Commander, the reporter is here.

779
44:31.926 --> 44:34.338
Oh! Look at the time.

780
44:34.338 --> 44:35.986
Chungseong! You're here?

781
44:35.986 --> 44:38.175
- Battalion Commander, long time no see. - Long time no see.

782
44:38.175 --> 44:40.970
- Have you eaten yet? - I'm starving.

783
44:40.970 --> 44:42.805
Then let's go. This way.

784
44:42.805 --> 44:44.326
Oh, wait.

785
44:44.326 --> 44:45.826
- 2nd Company Commander. - Yes, sir.

786
44:45.826 --> 44:47.780
I'm counting on you.

787
44:48.647 --> 44:51.946
And everything will work out.

788
44:51.946 --> 44:53.886
Thank you. Chungseong!

789
44:53.886 --> 44:55.306
Chungseong!

790
44:55.306 --> 44:56.947
Let's go!

791
44:56.947 --> 44:58.233
Hey.

792
44:59.406 --> 45:02.346
- Who was that? - Oh, he's a reporter for the Defense Daily.

793
45:02.346 --> 45:05.146
Really? A reporter for the Defense Daily?

794
45:05.146 --> 45:07.956
- Chungseong! I'll be going now. - Okay. Good work.

795
45:10.806 --> 45:15.382
What you see isn't everything, so don't hate me too much.

796
45:15.382 --> 45:17.056
Geez.

797
45:21.694 --> 45:23.046
Is everyone here?

798
45:23.046 --> 45:24.606
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

799
45:24.606 --> 45:25.876
Alright, smokers, raise your hands!

800
45:25.876 --> 45:27.886
- Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam! - Corporal Kim Dong Woo!

801
45:27.886 --> 45:30.366
- Private First Class Jeon Se Gye! - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

802
45:30.366 --> 45:33.126
- I'm not scolding you, so hands up! - Sergeant Kim Sang Hun!

803
45:33.126 --> 45:35.246
- Private Kim Han Sol! - Sergeant Kang Chan Seok!

804
45:35.246 --> 45:37.286
- Hey, Kyung Chae! - Corporal Lee Kyung Chae!

805
45:37.286 --> 45:40.381
- You smoke, don't you? - Yes, I do. Sorry!

806
45:40.381 --> 45:42.046
- Se Gye. - Private Jeon Se Gye!

807
45:42.046 --> 45:43.066
You didn't use to smoke.

808
45:43.066 --> 45:45.606
I used to smoke when I was working on a project, but I quit.

809
45:45.606 --> 45:48.120
But after working here, I couldn't help but start again.

810
45:48.120 --> 45:49.167
That's true.

811
45:49.167 --> 45:53.646
It's good to see you adjusting, but it's also a bit sad.

812
45:53.646 --> 45:55.964
- Hands down. - Hands down!

813
45:55.964 --> 45:57.925
What about Min Seok? Are you a non-smoker?

814
45:57.925 --> 46:00.166
I quit smoking a while back.

815
46:00.166 --> 46:02.104
Oh, that must be tough. How?

816
46:02.104 --> 46:05.261
Actually, during my last leave...

817
46:05.984 --> 46:07.984
I'm home!

818
46:16.566 --> 46:18.176
What time is it?

819
46:19.086 --> 46:21.536
11:20.

820
46:26.386 --> 46:28.356
11:21.

821
46:29.406 --> 46:31.526
Oh, a minute must have just passed.

822
46:31.526 --> 46:33.206
You're excited to be on leave, aren't you?

823
46:33.206 --> 46:37.826
I left on time, but I couldn't get a taxi, so I had to take the bus. That's why I'm late.

824
46:37.826 --> 46:39.886
What time did I tell you to be home?

825
46:39.886 --> 46:41.556
10:00.

826
46:42.706 --> 46:45.720
Come on, Sis. I'm not a kid anymore.

827
46:45.720 --> 46:46.906
[Dad's Phone Number]

828
46:46.906 --> 46:49.606
What? Dad? Go ahead and call him. I don't care.

829
46:49.606 --> 46:52.613
Dad told me to have a good time anyway.

830
46:58.886 --> 47:01.546
- Look at this little punk... - No, no, no! I'm serious!

831
47:01.546 --> 47:05.703
- I'm just tired from the PC cafe. - That's your excuse again?

832
47:09.286 --> 47:13.532
I think this punk forgot what I'm like.

833
47:16.917 --> 47:18.814
Get it together, Park Min Seok...

834
47:18.814 --> 47:24.426
I went to the bathhouse before coming home. No evidence.

835
47:24.426 --> 47:28.256
Even Park Min Ju won't be able to tell.

836
47:30.973 --> 47:34.596
I'm pretty tired, so I'm going to bed now.

837
47:35.288 --> 47:38.306
- Park Min Seok! - Corporal Park Min Seok!

838
48:14.475 --> 48:18.563
Look at this punk... They're not even domestic cigarettes...

839
48:24.466 --> 48:27.866
Those? Those belong to my friend. You know Je Uk, right?

840
48:27.866 --> 48:29.993
Je Uk asked me to hold onto them. Cho Je Uk.

841
48:29.993 --> 48:32.666
This punk lies every time he opens his mouth...

842
48:32.666 --> 48:34.870
I'm serious! Corporal Park Min Seok!

843
48:34.870 --> 48:37.164
If you smoke one more time,

844
48:37.164 --> 48:40.339
I'll make you burn incense in front of your own funeral photo.

845
48:46.716 --> 48:49.478
And that's why I quit.

846
48:50.316 --> 48:53.264
Yeah, if you don't want your life to end, you'd better quit smoking.

847
48:53.264 --> 48:54.265
Exactly.

848
48:54.265 --> 48:57.354
That's great motivation. We should invite her.

849
48:57.354 --> 48:59.921
No, no! You really can't!

850
49:01.556 --> 49:04.101
- Okay, attention. - Attention!

851
49:04.945 --> 49:07.374
This... I'm not sure how to say this.

852
49:08.571 --> 49:10.114
Today, the battalion commander...

853
49:10.114 --> 49:12.636
To be selected as a pilot unit for Barracks Reform 2.0...

854
49:12.636 --> 49:16.373
we will implement the "3S Movement" to stop unfair

855
49:16.373 --> 49:21.041
and unnecessary practices starting today.

856
49:21.041 --> 49:22.835
Regarding the 3S...

857
49:22.835 --> 49:26.670
The "S" stands for "STOP."

858
49:26.670 --> 49:29.287
In other words, stop!

859
49:30.121 --> 49:31.686
Stop!

860
49:32.333 --> 49:34.349
- Stop! - Yes...

861
49:35.536 --> 49:37.146
It's a movement.

862
49:37.959 --> 49:39.602
Through this 3S Movement,

863
49:39.602 --> 49:45.096
we'll stop everything that hinders combat power and stop laziness!

864
49:45.096 --> 49:47.821
By stopping inefficient waste,

865
49:47.821 --> 49:51.197
our members will be reborn

866
49:51.197 --> 49:55.026
as elite warriors optimized for victory.

867
49:55.704 --> 49:59.830
Let's all say it together. Stop!

868
49:59.830 --> 50:02.056
- Stop! - Stop!

869
50:02.056 --> 50:04.256
- Stop! - Stop!

870
50:04.256 --> 50:05.416
- Stop! - Stop!

871
50:05.416 --> 50:06.879
Good.

872
50:06.879 --> 50:09.506
The first part of this 3S Movement is being selected...

873
50:09.506 --> 50:12.036
As a smoking cessation pilot unit.

874
50:12.036 --> 50:15.906
He says we're starting the "Stop Smoking" movement.

875
50:17.586 --> 50:19.379
- Kyung Chae. - Corporal Lee Kyung Chae!

876
50:19.379 --> 50:21.076
You're discharging soon. You should quit.

877
50:21.076 --> 50:22.116
Does that even make sense?

878
50:22.116 --> 50:23.771
- What do we do? - We can't!

879
50:23.771 --> 50:25.064
"Stop smoking!"

880
50:25.064 --> 50:27.444
Hey, doesn't that sound like a guard's challenge?

881
50:27.444 --> 50:31.436
"Stop smoking! Stop! Stop! Lighters out. Nicotine, get out."

882
50:31.436 --> 50:34.281
Min Seok, don't push it.

883
50:34.281 --> 50:35.532
Sorry.

884
50:35.532 --> 50:37.076
This is ridiculous.

885
50:37.076 --> 50:41.333
3S? More like "Shit, Son of a bitch, Scared." That's 3S.

886
50:41.333 --> 50:42.756
Including officers.

887
50:42.756 --> 50:45.416
- What? - No, why?

888
50:45.416 --> 50:47.756
Now, I know this might seem like too much,

889
50:47.756 --> 50:51.301
and I know people said forced smoking cessation is a human rights violation,

890
50:51.301 --> 50:54.176
let's tough it out for a few days.

891
50:54.176 --> 50:55.886
So let's do it voluntarily!

892
50:55.886 --> 50:58.896
Instead of punishment, there will be rewards!

893
50:58.896 --> 51:03.049
If everyone in a barracks succeeds, the whole unit gets an overnight pass!

894
51:05.276 --> 51:07.096
Wait, we don't even smoke.

895
51:07.096 --> 51:08.266
We're at a disadvantage.

896
51:08.266 --> 51:13.240
Now, some non-smokers might think it's unfair that only smokers get a chance.

897
51:13.240 --> 51:14.283
Park Min Seok?

898
51:14.283 --> 51:18.396
- Corporal Park Min Seok! Yes, sir! - Oh, please.

899
51:18.396 --> 51:19.716
Am I wrong?

900
51:19.716 --> 51:24.096
So, if non-smokers help their barracks quit, they get a 2-day reward vacation!

901
51:24.096 --> 51:26.246
Oh, two days!

902
51:27.796 --> 51:30.096
You can report anyone you see smoking!

903
51:30.096 --> 51:32.050
Or you can help them quit!

904
51:32.050 --> 51:33.969
When you see someone smoking, shout,

905
51:33.969 --> 51:38.015
"Smoking! Stop! Stop! Stop!"

906
51:38.015 --> 51:42.182
It'll be more effective that way. Shall we try it together?

907
51:42.182 --> 51:45.811
Smoking! Stop! Stop! Stop!

908
51:45.811 --> 51:49.440
- Smoking! Stop! Stop! Stop! - Smoking! Stop! Stop! Stop!

909
51:49.440 --> 51:53.822
Right. Keep an eye on each other so everyone gets a reward, okay?

910
51:53.822 --> 51:55.536
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

911
51:55.536 --> 51:56.596
For what?

912
51:56.596 --> 51:58.911
We can't even get rewards...

913
51:58.911 --> 52:00.370
Everyone, be careful.

914
52:00.370 --> 52:03.436
Seriously, watch out. Smoking, stop! Stop! Stop!

915
52:03.436 --> 52:05.236
You want to die?

916
52:05.236 --> 52:06.976
Lighters out! Nicotine, get out!

917
52:06.976 --> 52:08.959
- Cigarettes out! - Min Seok.

918
52:08.959 --> 52:10.596
Corporal Park Min Seok?

919
52:10.596 --> 52:12.171
Don't push it.

920
52:12.956 --> 52:15.470
- I'm sorry. - I'm sorry.

921
52:15.470 --> 52:19.956
Also, we'll provide smoking cessation aids, so pick them up by the barracks.

922
52:19.956 --> 52:22.116
- Got it? - Yes, sir!

923
52:22.116 --> 52:25.100
I know Korea runs on school ties, regional ties, and smoking ties.

924
52:25.100 --> 52:27.747
But quitting isn't that hard!

925
52:27.747 --> 52:29.608
Just skip that first one when you wake up!

926
52:29.608 --> 52:31.516
I'm screwed. I won't be able to poop.

927
52:31.516 --> 52:34.860
- I'll get constipated immediately. - And skip the one after meals!

928
52:34.860 --> 52:37.796
Company Commander! You're telling us to give up our digestive medicine!

929
52:37.796 --> 52:40.994
Skip the one with vending machine coffee!

930
52:40.994 --> 52:43.622
Skip the one after having ramen after your shift!

931
52:43.622 --> 52:46.375
Just skip the ones during work breaks. Got it?

932
52:46.375 --> 52:48.323
Company Commander, that's too cruel!

933
52:48.323 --> 52:52.536
A smoke after work is the best part!

934
52:52.536 --> 52:55.121
It'll be the death of you, man.

935
52:55.121 --> 52:58.808
If everyone succeeds and gets an overnight pass,

936
52:58.808 --> 53:01.431
I'll buy chicken!

937
53:01.431 --> 53:03.544
Oh! Chicken!

938
53:05.486 --> 53:08.313
- Good luck, everyone! - Good luck!

939
53:08.313 --> 53:09.808
Dismissed!

940
53:13.068 --> 53:16.979
Um, First Sergeant... Do we have to quit too?

941
53:16.979 --> 53:20.756
Aren't you part of 2nd Company? Of course you do!

942
53:20.756 --> 53:26.556
If I'd met a battalion commander like him back then, I'd be a movie star by now.

943
53:26.556 --> 53:27.791
I'm definitely quitting now.

944
53:27.791 --> 53:31.396
I think being a movie star would've been tough even if you'd quit smoking.

945
53:31.396 --> 53:34.076
Hey, Il Gu. You should quit while you're young.

946
53:34.076 --> 53:36.876
Don't end up like me and regret it later.

947
53:36.876 --> 53:39.598
- Yes, sir. - Take care, sir.

948
53:43.836 --> 53:46.666
Do you know how old the First Sergeant is?

949
53:47.396 --> 53:49.776
Um... Isn't he in his 50s?

950
53:49.776 --> 53:51.982
He looks about the same age as my father.

951
53:51.982 --> 53:53.981
He's 40.

952
53:53.981 --> 53:56.196
39 in international age.

953
53:56.196 --> 53:59.016
What? He's only in his 40s?

954
53:59.016 --> 54:00.396
Wow, that's insane...

955
54:00.396 --> 54:04.226
I'm definitely quitting smoking starting today...

956
54:08.456 --> 54:09.913
Are you going to try?

957
54:09.913 --> 54:11.293
Just for a few days!

958
54:11.293 --> 54:14.558
Great! It's worth a shot, isn't it?

959
54:14.558 --> 54:17.596
It's totally worth it! It's our first group overnight pass. I'd definitely quit for that.

960
54:17.596 --> 54:20.841
Before Sergeant Kang Chan Seok and Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam are discharged,

961
54:20.841 --> 54:24.016
wouldn't it be great if we all went out on an overnight pass together?

962
54:24.016 --> 54:26.296
I think that would be really great!

963
54:26.296 --> 54:28.266
Can I really hold out?

964
54:29.269 --> 54:30.771
I can't do it.

965
54:30.771 --> 54:33.357
Forget quitting. You guys go without me.

966
54:33.357 --> 54:35.432
Let's go have a smoke.

967
54:36.316 --> 54:39.208
Sergeant Choi, Sergeant Kang.

968
54:39.208 --> 54:42.836
May I say one thing?

969
54:43.780 --> 54:44.910
Go ahead.

970
54:44.910 --> 54:50.091
I've never been on a group pass, so I really want us all to go together.

971
54:51.200 --> 54:54.740
It'll be hard to see Se Gye after discharge, so let's all go out together just once!

972
54:54.740 --> 54:58.090
Please, just give it a try once.

973
54:58.090 --> 55:01.500
True. We should make some memories with Se Gye, right?

974
55:07.140 --> 55:08.767
Please...

975
55:08.767 --> 55:11.892
Okay! I'm motivated now. Let's go!

976
55:11.892 --> 55:14.600
- Thank you! - All right, let's do this!

977
55:14.600 --> 55:16.880
Yes! Sounds good!

978
55:16.880 --> 55:20.279
Today's duty roster is out. Please check and sign. That's all.

979
55:20.279 --> 55:21.880
I'll go check it right away!

980
55:21.880 --> 55:24.710
He's fast. Let's have a smoke before we go back in.

981
55:24.710 --> 55:26.753
Hey, what are you doing? Seriously!

982
55:26.753 --> 55:28.947
- Man, I almost blew it in one minute. - You can't do that.

983
55:28.947 --> 55:31.248
Sorry. I'll go get some coffee instead.

984
55:31.248 --> 55:34.552
- Coffee is dangerous too. - You can't have coffee and a smoke!

985
55:35.749 --> 55:39.720
I've never even tried quitting. Why are we suddenly a pilot unit?

986
55:39.720 --> 55:43.022
Whatever. They're giving us leave, so let's just try to quit!

987
55:43.022 --> 55:44.049
Yes, sir!

988
55:44.049 --> 55:47.817
- So, are Hyeon Uk and I the only smokers? - Yes, that's right.

989
55:48.580 --> 55:51.850
Sergeant Kim Sang Hun, you can definitely quit too.

990
55:53.700 --> 55:56.979
Ugh... It's so noisy I can't even sleep.

991
55:56.979 --> 56:00.448
They say never to trust a guy who quits smoking.

992
56:00.448 --> 56:03.060
Park Min Seok is quite tough.

993
56:03.060 --> 56:06.940
Well, I'm a bit of a bulldozer once I set my mind to something.

994
56:06.940 --> 56:10.579
You're not a bulldozer. You look like a bulldog.

995
56:10.579 --> 56:12.750
Hey, why are you like this?

996
56:12.750 --> 56:15.669
And why do you always come here?

997
56:16.320 --> 56:19.420
- I feel comfortable here. - Well, we don't.

998
56:19.420 --> 56:23.640
Man, you're so mean! Seriously, give us some space.

999
56:23.640 --> 56:27.095
But why do the officers have to quit smoking too?

1000
56:27.095 --> 56:28.722
To lead by example.

1001
56:28.722 --> 56:31.930
Shut up. Screw that. I'm going to smoke in secret.

1002
56:31.930 --> 56:36.230
We don't even get leave. Why the hell are we doing this?

1003
56:38.649 --> 56:41.568
What have you been staring at?

1004
56:41.568 --> 56:46.114
I'm just glad to see the old Sergeant Choi Il Gu back.

1005
56:46.114 --> 56:50.374
Shut it. My life right now is worse than a private's.

1006
56:51.900 --> 56:54.289
- Hey, Choi Il Gu! - Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu!

1007
56:54.289 --> 56:55.760
Do you still think you're a soldier?

1008
56:55.760 --> 56:58.780
- Get your head in the game! - I'm sorry, sir.

1009
56:58.780 --> 57:01.585
A lowly staff sergeant wants to go rest just because he was on duty?

1010
57:01.585 --> 57:05.726
Unbelievable. Where do you think you're going, junior? Get back to work.

1011
57:05.726 --> 57:09.179
- Yes, sir. - Hey, do you know how to play Lineage?

1012
57:09.179 --> 57:11.595
- I'm on duty today, so level me up. - Yes, sir...

1013
57:11.595 --> 57:14.284
I'll have a drink in your room later, so clean it up.

1014
57:14.284 --> 57:15.609
Yes, sir.

1015
57:15.609 --> 57:17.059
- Do you understand, Choi Il Gu? - Yes, sir.

1016
57:17.059 --> 57:18.100
- Choi Il Gu! - Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu!

1017
57:18.100 --> 57:19.340
- Choi Il Gu! - Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu!

1018
57:19.340 --> 57:21.500
- I'm sorry. - Get it together.

1019
57:21.500 --> 57:23.862
- I'm sorry. - Choi Il Gu! Hey!

1020
57:23.862 --> 57:28.760
- Choi Il Gu! - Choi Il Gu!

1021
57:28.760 --> 57:31.230
Wake up, Choi Il Gu!

1022
57:37.100 --> 57:39.300
Are you crying?

1023
57:39.300 --> 57:41.044
It's sweat. Just sweat.

1024
57:41.044 --> 57:43.860
Man, I'm suddenly craving a smoke so bad.

1025
57:43.860 --> 57:47.360
I've never tried quitting before. I'm in big trouble.

1026
57:47.360 --> 57:49.918
- Should I call my sister for you? - Hey, are you kidding me?

1027
57:49.918 --> 57:51.263
Sorry.

1028
57:51.263 --> 57:54.354
You know... I actually tried quitting once.

1029
57:55.434 --> 57:58.103
Day one, my hands started shaking.

1030
57:58.103 --> 58:01.647
Day two, I couldn't poop. And then day three...

1031
58:02.400 --> 58:06.311
My whole body started trembling.

1032
58:07.943 --> 58:11.500
- I had chills and cold sweats. - That's right.

1033
58:11.500 --> 58:15.760
Then another day passed, and on day four...

1034
58:15.760 --> 58:19.208
Ni-ni-nicotine...

1035
58:19.208 --> 58:22.340
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu! Are you okay?

1036
58:22.340 --> 58:24.910
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu!

1037
58:26.507 --> 58:28.459
I blacked out.

1038
58:29.172 --> 58:31.180
So I realized I couldn't go on.

1039
58:31.180 --> 58:34.594
I got nicotine gum and chewed it like crazy whenever I had a craving.

1040
58:34.594 --> 58:37.768
Then the withdrawal symptoms vanished.

1041
58:37.768 --> 58:39.220
So you successfully quit?

1042
58:39.220 --> 58:42.022
I did back then! But...

1043
58:42.022 --> 58:46.200
I quit smoking only to get addicted to the nicotine gum.

1044
58:46.200 --> 58:48.240
So, I tried to cut back on the gum.

1045
58:48.240 --> 58:50.313
Day one, my hands started shaking.

1046
58:50.313 --> 58:52.180
Day two, I couldn't poop again.

1047
58:52.180 --> 58:54.030
And on day three...

1048
58:55.365 --> 58:59.544
Chills and cold sweats everywhere.

1049
58:59.544 --> 59:01.500
So what did you do?

1050
59:01.500 --> 59:03.928
To quit the nicotine gum...

1051
59:03.928 --> 59:06.301
I quit quitting smoking.

1052
59:08.180 --> 59:10.740
Isn't that hilarious?

1053
59:10.740 --> 59:13.846
I chewed nicotine gum to quit smoking, but I got addicted to the gum,

1054
59:13.846 --> 59:18.036
so I smoked again to quit the gum. It's so funny!

1055
59:20.557 --> 59:22.900
Park Min Seok, your fake laugh is so obvious.

1056
59:22.900 --> 59:26.024
No, it's not. It was a funny story.

1057
59:26.024 --> 59:29.065
Anyway, you guys try it too. Tell me how it goes.

1058
59:29.065 --> 59:30.525
Yes, sir.

1059
59:30.525 --> 59:34.460
- That's very encouraging. - Right. Good luck.

1060
59:34.460 --> 59:36.312
Wait, where are you going?

1061
59:39.680 --> 59:42.374
Man, I'm so jealous.

1062
59:42.374 --> 59:45.580
Reporting for duty! Stop smoking! Stop! Stop!

1063
59:45.580 --> 59:48.050
Lighters out! Cigarettes out!

1064
59:49.440 --> 59:54.041
- Min Seok, let's take this outside! - I beg your pardon?

1065
59:56.313 --> 59:58.152
You reap what you sow.

1066
59:59.600 --> 01:00:01.705
It's karma...

1067
01:00:18.620 --> 01:00:21.240
Geez. Are you trying to sink the floor with those sighs?

1068
01:00:21.240 --> 01:00:24.082
Huh? How did you know I was here?

1069
01:00:24.082 --> 01:00:29.288
I heard a sigh from outside, and it sounded so familiar that I had to come find you.

1070
01:00:29.288 --> 01:00:33.240
Is that so?

1071
01:00:33.240 --> 01:00:35.680
So, what's the matter?

1072
01:00:35.680 --> 01:00:38.677
For the soldiers, this will be scarier than actual war.

1073
01:00:38.677 --> 01:00:41.284
They survive military life on cigarettes,

1074
01:00:41.284 --> 01:00:44.724
but now they're just fuming inside. Man.

1075
01:00:44.724 --> 01:00:46.418
Tell me about it.

1076
01:00:46.418 --> 01:00:49.270
But what can we do? Orders are orders.

1077
01:00:50.340 --> 01:00:53.015
Oh! I heard you're up for promotion.

1078
01:00:53.015 --> 01:00:56.580
Was that in the Defense Daily or what?

1079
01:00:56.580 --> 01:00:59.120
How does everyone know about it?

1080
01:01:00.060 --> 01:01:03.540
This is your last chance, right?

1081
01:01:03.540 --> 01:01:06.785
Yeah. I'm not expecting much.

1082
01:01:06.785 --> 01:01:09.663
Don't worry. It'll work out.

1083
01:01:11.580 --> 01:01:15.968
Worrying won't change the outcome, whether it's good or bad.

1084
01:01:15.968 --> 01:01:19.166
I'm not worried, nor am I expecting anything.

1085
01:01:24.268 --> 01:01:27.078
It's my fault for not going to the academy.

1086
01:01:28.240 --> 01:01:30.566
- You know what? - What?

1087
01:01:30.566 --> 01:01:35.357
Even if you had gone to the academy, you still...

1088
01:01:36.977 --> 01:01:38.612
wouldn't get promoted.

1089
01:01:40.360 --> 01:01:42.640
Bingo!

1090
01:01:42.640 --> 01:01:45.580
In the army, you just do as you're told, but you're too sincere! That's why!

1091
01:01:45.580 --> 01:01:48.417
Oh? Bingo again!

1092
01:01:48.417 --> 01:01:50.107
Let's eat.

1093
01:01:51.958 --> 01:01:54.899
- Is this your treat? - We're splitting the bill.

1094
01:01:54.899 --> 01:01:56.884
See? The academy isn't the problem.

1095
01:01:56.884 --> 01:01:59.424
Goodness.

1096
01:01:59.424 --> 01:02:01.478
- Let's toast. - Yes.

1097
01:02:04.100 --> 01:02:06.102
Why'd you order so much for yourself?

1098
01:02:06.102 --> 01:02:07.420
This is a single serving.

1099
01:02:07.420 --> 01:02:09.480
This? No way.

1100
01:02:09.480 --> 01:02:12.890
Actually, I knew you'd come. I ordered for two.

1101
01:02:13.700 --> 01:02:17.960
That's touching, but aren't you being a bit too blunt with the facts?

1102
01:02:17.960 --> 01:02:19.850
What facts?

1103
01:02:21.940 --> 01:02:23.620
- Thank you. - For what?

1104
01:02:23.620 --> 01:02:25.642
Just... for everything.

1105
01:02:46.180 --> 01:02:47.840
Son.

1106
01:02:47.840 --> 01:02:49.560
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

1107
01:02:49.560 --> 01:02:52.231
Take it back. Do it.

1108
01:02:52.231 --> 01:02:54.795
I learned that you can't take back a move in Omok.

1109
01:02:54.795 --> 01:02:58.460
- Take it back. - You're being so unfair.

1110
01:02:58.460 --> 01:03:00.447
- Bit Na Ri. - Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri.

1111
01:03:00.447 --> 01:03:02.737
- Win for me. - Yes, sir.

1112
01:03:02.737 --> 01:03:04.964
If you lose, you're summoned.

1113
01:03:04.964 --> 01:03:06.810
If you win, I'll treat you to the PX.

1114
01:03:06.810 --> 01:03:09.248
I will win no matter what!

1115
01:03:09.248 --> 01:03:10.920
How do you lose every time?

1116
01:03:10.920 --> 01:03:12.770
He's just too good.

1117
01:03:15.295 --> 01:03:17.040
I'm heading out for duty.

1118
01:03:17.040 --> 01:03:19.660
- Have a good one. - Okay, see you.

1119
01:03:19.660 --> 01:03:23.260
If I win, can I go to the PX too?

1120
01:03:23.260 --> 01:03:26.663
- Sure, the PX. - Think you can do it? You confident?

1121
01:03:26.663 --> 01:03:29.573
- Yes, I'm confident! - Okay.

